Fibonacci Fruitcake.

A fruitcake that climbs the golden ladder. Ask the kitchen for a number of
raisins, and it chops them one at a time; with every raisin the flour and the
sugar shuffle one rung further up the Fibonacci sequence. Serve the flour.
The nutmeg oil, the quince juice and the sparkling water are only there for
the prompt - Chef prints its baking dishes from the top down, so the garnish
goes in last and comes out first.

Ingredients.
78 ml nutmeg oil
63 ml quince juice
32 ml sparkling water
0 g flour
1 g sugar
raisins

Method.
Take raisins from refrigerator.
Chop the raisins.
Put flour into the mixing bowl.
Add sugar to the mixing bowl.
Put sugar into the mixing bowl.
Fold flour into the mixing bowl.
Fold sugar into the mixing bowl.
Chop the raisins until chopped.
Put flour into the mixing bowl.
Put sparkling water into the mixing bowl.
Put quince juice into the mixing bowl.
Put nutmeg oil into the mixing bowl.
Pour contents of the mixing bowl into the baking dish.

Serves 1.

